Round 2 is complete. I fixed the low-risk evidence and wiring issues: `native_rdma/control_plane/app.py` now treats baseline/raw result files as executed evidence and keeps `launched_from_dashboard` separate, `performances/run_all.py` can refresh `performances/summary.md` from existing PF raw files, `performances/run_all.sh` now refreshes that summary after a full run, the demo JS defaults no longer hardcode `localhost`, and `dashboard/README.md` now matches the live `/api/demo3|5|6` and status endpoints. I also updated `.ai/pipeline/state.md`; `BLOCKED` and `DONE` are absent.

Changed files: `native_rdma/control_plane/app.py`, `performances/run_all.py`, `performances/run_all.sh`, `performances/summary.md`, `dashboard/m7_route.js`, `dashboard/m8_isolation.js`, `dashboard/m9_ha.js`, `dashboard/m10_capture.js`, `dashboard/README.md`, `.ai/pipeline/state.md`.

Validation: `python3 -m py_compile native_rdma/control_plane/*.py performances/run_all.py`, `bash -n functions/run_all.sh performances/run_all.sh`, `node --check dashboard/m7_route.js dashboard/m8_isolation.js dashboard/m9_ha.js dashboard/m10_capture.js`, `python3 performances/run_all.py --refresh-summary`, `git diff --check ...`, plus Flask smoke checks showing `/`, `/function-dashboard/`, `/performance-dashboard/`, `/api/functions/summary`, and `/api/performance/summary` all returned 200. The summary APIs now report `executed=17, pending=0` for functions and `executed=9, pending=0` for performance.

Remaining Round 3 work: peer readback failures in `rdma/FN-3`, `rdma/FN-5`, `mempool/FN-4`; PF-1/PF-3/PF-4/PF-6; the `rdma/FN-1` CLI mode gap; and the host-side hardware path decision.
